.75 2h3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-3.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.=
25h8.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v3.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 12.=
25 14h-8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 2 12.25v-8.5C2 2.784 2.784 2 3.75 2Zm6.854-1h4.1=
46a.25.25 0 0 1 .25.25v4.146a.25.25 0 0 1-.427.177L13.03 4.03 9.28 7.78a.75=
1.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042l3.75-3.75-1.543-1.543A.25.2=
5 0 0 1 10.604 1Z"></path></svg></a> is the software on Quest that manages =
and allocates requests for compute resources. Users submit computational =
=E2=80=9Cjobs=E2=80=9D to Quest requesting the CPUs, nodes, memory, and oth=
er resources they need.  Slurm manages these requests and allocates resourc=
es to jobs as they are available.</p>
<p>Jobs that run without user supervision are called <strong>batch jobs</st=
rong>.  Jobs where the user will actively use an application with the reque=
sted compute resources are called <strong>interactive jobs</strong>.</p>
<p>Slurm decides which jobs to run when based on the requested resources an=
d your <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwes=
tern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com=
#fairshare">Fairshare score</a>, which takes into account the priority of y=
our Slurm account and your past usage of Quest.</p>
<div class=3D"admonition tip">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Tip</p>
<p>A few common misconceptions about batch jobs:</p>
<ol class=3D"arabic simple">
<li><p>We don=E2=80=99t actually aim for 100% efficiency. Job resources can=
 fluctuate and we don=E2=80=99t want the job to run out of memory. We often=
 aim for 75% efficiency.</p></li>
<li><p>More memory doesn=E2=80=99t always mean a faster job. There are many=
 factors that influence how long a job runs for. Our team is happy to help =
if you have any questions.</p></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id=3D"the-job-submission-script">
<span id=3D"id1"></span><h2>The Job Submission Script<a class=3D"headerlink=
" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slu=
rm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#the-job-submission-script" title=3D"=
Link to this heading">#</a></h2>
<p>Slurm requires users to write a submission script to run a batch job.  I=
t is a Bash script that specifies what resources the job needs to run, how =
to handle output and errors, and what commands to run as part of the job.</=
p>
<section id=3D"example-submission-script">
<span id=3D"example-script"></span><h3>Example Submission Script<a class=3D=
"headerlink" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/use=
r-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#example-submission-script=
" title=3D"Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
<p>Create a <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre=
">.sh</span></code> file for the submission script.  The file will have <co=
de class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span=
></code> statements at the top that give Slurm the information it needs to =
schedule and run the job.  After that, you can enter commands to load data,=
 run code files, or do the other work of the job.</p>
<p>In all examples, <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span clas=
s=3D"pre">&lt;&gt;</span></code> denotes a value that you need to fill in. =
 Fill in these values and remove the <code class=3D"docutils literal notran=
slate"><span class=3D"pre">&lt;&gt;</span></code>.</p>
<p><strong>Example: <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span clas=
s=3D"pre">jobscript.sh</span></code></strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell0" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"ch">#!/bin/bash<=
/span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --account=3D&lt;account_id&gt;  ## Required: you=
r Slurm account ID, i.e. eXXXX, pXXXX or bXXXX</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --partition=3D&lt;partition&gt; ## Required: buy=
in, short, normal, long, gengpu, genhimem, etc.</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --time=3D&lt;HH:MM:SS&gt;       ## Required: How=
 long will the job need to run?  Limits vary by partition</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --nodes=3D&lt;#&gt;             ## How many comp=
uters/nodes do you need? Usually 1</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --ntasks=3D&lt;#&gt;            ## How many CPUs=
 or processors do you need? (default value 1)</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --mem=3D&lt;#G&gt;              ## How much RAM =
do you need per computer/node? G =3D gigabytes</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --job-name=3D&lt;name&gt;       ## Used to ident=
ify the job </span>

<span class=3D"c1"># load any modules needed</span>
module<span class=3D"w"> </span>load<span class=3D"w"> </span>mamba/24.3.0

<span class=3D"c1"># set or change your working directory if needed</span>
<span class=3D"nb">cd</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>~/myscripts

<span class=3D"c1"># run any commands or code files</span>
date
python<span class=3D"w"> </span>--version
python<span class=3D"w"> </span>-c<span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"=
s2">"print('hello')"</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell0">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>The first line of the script, <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslat=
e"><span class=3D"pre">#!/bin/bash</span></code>, loads the Bash shell; it =
is required. Only the lines that begin with <code class=3D"docutils literal=
 notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span></code> are interpreted by =
Slurm at the time of job submission. Normally in Bash, <code class=3D"docut=
ils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#</span></code> is a comment c=
haracter which means that anything written after a <code class=3D"docutils =
literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#</span></code> is ignored by the =
Bash interpreter/language. When writing a submission script, however, the S=
lurm interpreter recognizes <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><s=
pan class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span></code> as a command.  Any words following =
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">##</span><=
/code> on the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"p=
re">#SBATCH</span></code> lines are treated as comments and ignored by Slur=
m interpreter.</p>
<p>Once Slurm places the job on a compute node, the remainder of the script=
 (everything after the last <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><s=
pan class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span></code> line) is run. After the Slurm comma=
nds, the rest of the script works like a regular Bash script. You can modif=
y environment variables, load modules, change directories, and execute prog=
ram commands. Lines in the second half of the script that start with <code =
class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#</span></code> =
are comments, such as <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span cl=
ass=3D"pre">#</span> <span class=3D"pre">load</span> <span class=3D"pre">an=
y</span> <span class=3D"pre">modules</span> <span class=3D"pre">needed</spa=
n></code> in the the example above.</p>
<p>Example values for <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span cl=
ass=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span></code> options:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell1" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --ac=
count=3Dp00000      ## use your Slurm account name</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --partition=3Dshort</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --time=3D01:00:00       ## one hour</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --nodes=3D1             ## 1 node</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --ntasks=3D1            ## 1 processor</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --mem=3D2G              ## 2 GB of RAM</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --job-name=3Dsample_job  </span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell1">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p>More information on how to choose the values of the Slurm options is in =
<a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.ed=
u/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#slurm-=
options">Slurm Configuration Settings</a>.</p>
<div class=3D"admonition note">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Note</p>
<p>The compute and memory resources you request affect your <a class=3D"ref=
erence internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest=
/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#fairshare">Fairshare<=
/a> score.  Request only what you need for your job.</p>
</div>
<div class=3D"admonition tip">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Tip</p>
<p>There are additional example job submission scripts in the <a class=3D"r=
eference external" href=3D"https://github.com/nuitrcs/examplejobs/tree/mast=
er/job-array" target=3D"_blank">RCDS Example Job Repository on GitHub <svg =
version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D"1.0em" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria=
