ummary><div class=3D"sd-summary-content sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">There is a secondary mechanism that starts lower =
priority jobs on resources
reserved by higher priority jobs while the higher priority jobs are acquiri=
ng their
full set of resources. This is called backfill scheduling which helps
to increase the utilization of the compute nodes and guarantees no delay
in starting the higher priority jobs. To benefit from this mechanism, it
is important to accurately request resources (wall time, core, memory)
so that the scheduler can find appropriate space on the cluster for your jo=
b.
Use the <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwe=
stern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/job-profiling/job-profiling.html#jobstat=
s-tool"><span class=3D"std std-ref"><code class=3D"docutils literal notrans=
late"><span class=3D"pre">jobstats</span></code></span></a> command to get =
information about your job=E2=80=99s resource utilization.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">From time to time, compute resources cannot be ba=
ckfilled effectively and nodes/cores may appear idle while jobs are waiting=
 on the queue.</p>
</div>
</details></section>
<section id=3D"partitions">
<span id=3D"id2"></span><h2>Partitions<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https=
://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?u=
tm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#partitions" title=3D"Link to this heading">#</a></h=
2>
<p>All jobs must specify a partition.  Partitions determine which compute n=
odes the job can be scheduled on.</p>
<section id=3D"general-access-partitions">
<h3>General Access Partitions<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://rcdsdo=
cs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=
=3Dchatgpt.com#general-access-partitions" title=3D"Link to this heading">#<=
/a></h3>
<p>Partitions that run on regular compute nodes without special resources.<=
/p>
<div class=3D"pst-scrollable-table-container" tabindex=3D"-1"><table class=
=3D"table">
<thead>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><th class=3D"head"><p>Partition</p></th>
<th class=3D"head"><p>Minimum Wall Time<br>HH:MM:SS</p></th>
<th class=3D"head"><p>Maximum Wall Time<br>HH:MM:SS</p></th>
<th class=3D"head"><p>Notes</p></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p>short</p></td>
<td><p>00:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>04:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>For jobs that will run in 4 hours or less. The short partition has a=
ccess to most compute nodes on Quest.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><td><p>normal</p></td>
<td><p>04:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>48:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>For jobs that will run between 4 hours and 2 days. The normal partit=
ion has access to more compute nodes than the long partition but fewer than=
 the short partition.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p>long</p></td>
<td><p>48:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>168:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>The long partition is for jobs that will run between 2 days and 7 da=
ys. The long partition has access to fewer compute nodes than the short and=
 normal partitions.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Jobs scheduled on the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span=
 class=3D"pre">short</span></code> partition typically start the soonest du=
e to the greater number of compute nodes available and the shorter time req=
uired.  Consider splitting up jobs to run in less than 4 hours when possibl=
e.</p>
<p>If you have a General Access compute resource and need to run jobs longe=
r than one week, contact <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"mailto:que=
st-help%40northwestern.edu?subject=3DQuest%20Long-running%20job" target=3D"=
_blank">quest-help<span>@</span>northwestern<span>.</span>edu <svg version=
=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D"1.0em" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-hidden=
=3D"true" style=3D"display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; fill: cur=
rentColor;"><path d=3D"M3.75 2h3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-3.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25=
.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h8.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 =
0v3.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 12.25 14h-8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 2 12.25v-8.5C2 2.784 2.=
784 2 3.75 2Zm6.854-1h4.146a.25.25 0 0 1 .25.25v4.146a.25.25 0 0 1-.427.177=
L13.03 4.03 9.28 7.78a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042l3.=
75-3.75-1.543-1.543A.25.25 0 0 1 10.604 1Z"></path></svg></a> for a consult=
ation. Some special accommodations can be made for jobs requiring the resou=
rces of up to a single node for a month or less.</p>
<p>Partitions that run on specialty compute nodes with GPU or high-memory r=
esources.</p>
<div class=3D"pst-scrollable-table-container" tabindex=3D"-1"><table class=
=3D"table">
<thead>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><th class=3D"head"><p>Partition</p></th>
<th class=3D"head"><p>Maximum Wall Time<br>HH:MM:SS</p></th>
<th class=3D"head"><p>Notes</p></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p>gengpu</p></td>
<td><p>48:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>Only for jobs requiring GPUs. In addition to entering <em>gengpu</em=
> as the partition in the submission script, the script must specify <code =
class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <=
span class=3D"pre">--gres=3Dgpu:a100:X</span></code>, where <code class=3D"=
docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">X</span></code> is the nu=
mber of GPUs required. See <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://=
rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/gpu/gpu.html#gpus-on-=
quest"><span class=3D"std std-ref">GPUs on Quest</span></a> for details.</p=
></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><td><p>genhimem</p></td>
<td><p>48:00:00</p></td>
<td><p>Only for jobs requiring more than 473 GB memory per node. This parti=
tion has access to a 52-core node with 1480 GB of schedulable memory.</p></=
td>
</tr>
