</div>
<p>The wall time limits vary by partition. Priority Access resources have d=
ifferent wall time limits as well.</p>
<p>Some Slurm accounts, such as the <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D=
"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/gcc/using-gcc.html#gcc"=
><span class=3D"std std-ref">GCC Slurm account, b1042</span></a>, have addi=
tional <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwes=
tern.edu/systems/quest/gcc/using-gcc.html#gcc-partitions"><span class=3D"st=
d std-ref">partition names</span></a>.  If your account has account-specifi=
c partitions, use those partition names instead of the account name or =E2=
=80=9Cbuyin.=E2=80=9D</p>
<div class=3D"admonition warning">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Warning</p>
<p>Slurm accounts associated with Priority Access compute resources cannot =
use the General Access partitions.</p>
