<section id=3D"slurm-configuration-settings">
<span id=3D"slurm-options"></span><h2>Slurm Configuration Settings<a class=
=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/=
user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#slurm-configuration-se=
ttings" title=3D"Link to this heading">#</a></h2>
<p>There are many options and settings available when submitting a job beyo=
nd the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SB=
ATCH</span></code> options shown in the <a class=3D"reference internal" hre=
f=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/sl=
urm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#example-script">example submission script=
</a>.  Common options, their possible values, and considerations for choosi=
ng appropriate values are listed here.</p>
<div class=3D"admonition tip">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Tip</p>
<p>Slurm offers two methods, one short (such as <code class=3D"docutils lit=
eral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">-A</span></code>) and one long/verbos=
e (<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--accou=
nt</span></code>) to indicate most settings. For the long option name, an <=
code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">=3D</span><=
/code> sign is required after the flag (ex. <code class=3D"docutils literal=
 notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--account=3Dp00000</span></code>).</p>
</div>
