/span><span class=3D"sd-summary-state-marker sd-summary-chevron-right"><svg=
 version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" height=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-oc=
ticon-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"=
M8.72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44 12 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.04=
2.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.75.75 =
0 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></summary><div class=3D"sd-summary-conte=
nt sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">-N</span></code>/<code class=3D"docutils literal notran=
slate"><span class=3D"pre">--nodes</span></code> option specifies how many =
nodes (computers) are needed.  This is an optional but strongly recommended=
 setting. It should be set to 1 unless your code is specifically designed t=
o use multinode protocols such as MPI.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell11" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --n=
odes=3D&lt;number_of_nodes&gt;</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell11">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<div class=3D"admonition warning">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Warning</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The vast majority of software can only run on a s=
ingle node and cannot run across multiple nodes. If <code class=3D"docutils=
 literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--nodes</span></code> is not set,=
 but <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--nta=
sks</span></code> (number of cores) is greater than 1, Slurm may match the =
job with cores on different nodes.  Only applications specifically designed=
 to use multiple nodes can successfully use cores from different nodes.</p>
</div>
</div>
</details><details class=3D"sd-sphinx-override sd-dropdown sd-card sd-mb-3"=
 id=3D"opt-cores">
<summary class=3D"sd-summary-title sd-card-header">
<span class=3D"sd-summary-icon"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=
=3D"1.0em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octicon-note" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-=
hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 3.75C0 2.784.784 2 1.75 2h12.5c.966 0 1.75.78=
4 1.75 1.75v8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 14H1.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 12.25Zm1.75=
-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h12.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v=
-8.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25ZM3.5 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75h7a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1=
.5h-7a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75Zm.75 2.25h4a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-4a.75.75 0 0 1 0=
-1.5Z"></path></svg></span><span class=3D"sd-summary-text">Number of Cores<=
/span><span class=3D"sd-summary-state-marker sd-summary-chevron-right"><svg=
 version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" height=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-oc=
ticon-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"=
M8.72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44 12 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.04=
2.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.75.75 =
0 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></summary><div class=3D"sd-summary-conte=
nt sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">-n/--ntasks</span></code> option specifies how many cor=
es are needed. Only request more than 1 core if your application can make u=
se of them through parallelization. There are two predominant types of para=
llelization and depending on which method your application uses, you will e=
ither request cores <em>with</em> the <code class=3D"docutils literal notra=
nslate"><span class=3D"pre">-N/--nodes</span></code> option or request core=
s <em>without</em> the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span c=
lass=3D"pre">-N/--nodes</span></code> option.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Applications using shared memory parallelization =
(OpenMP, R=E2=80=99s doParallel, Python=E2=80=99s multiprocessing, MATLAB l=
ocal parpool, etc.) can only utilize CPUs <em>within a single node/computer=
</em> and CPUs allocated <em>across</em> multiple computers will go unused.=
 In this situation, <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span clas=
s=3D"pre">--nodes=3D1</span></code> <em>must</em> be set along with <code c=
lass=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--ntasks</span></=
code>.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell12" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --n=
odes=3D1</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --ntasks=3D&lt;number_of_cores&gt;</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell12">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Applications using Message Passing Interface (MPI=
) can utilize cores (CPUs) allocated <em>across</em> nodes/computers. In th=
is situation, <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"p=
re">-n/--ntasks</span></code> should be used <em>without</em> setting the <=
code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">-N/--nodes<=
/span></code> option.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell13" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --n=
tasks=3D&lt;number_of_cores&gt;</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell13">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<div class=3D"admonition warning">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Warning</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><spa=
n class=3D"pre">--ntasks</span></code> can allocate cores on different node=
s.  Only applications using Message Passing Interface (MPI) can use cores a=
nd share memory across multiple nodes.</p>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Before requesting a given number of cores on a si=
ngle node, please consider how many cores are available on each of the <a c=
lass=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/sy=
stems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#schedulabl=
e-resources">different generations/families of compute nodes</a> that make =
up Quest. For example, <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span c=
lass=3D"pre">quest12</span></code> nodes have 64 cores per node, while <cod=
e class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">quest13</span>=
</code> and <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre=
">quest14</span></code> nodes have 128 cores per node each.  Requesting a l=
arge number of cores per node can limit the number of compute nodes on whic=
h the job can be scheduled.</p>
</div>
</details><details class=3D"sd-sphinx-override sd-dropdown sd-card sd-mb-3"=
 id=3D"opt-memory">
<summary class=3D"sd-summary-title sd-card-header">
<span class=3D"sd-summary-icon"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=
=3D"1.0em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octicon-note" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-=
hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 3.75C0 2.784.784 2 1.75 2h12.5c.966 0 1.75.78=
4 1.75 1.75v8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 14H1.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 12.25Zm1.75=
-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h12.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v=
-8.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25ZM3.5 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75h7a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1=
.5h-7a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75Zm.75 2.25h4a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-4a.75.75 0 0 1 0=
-1.5Z"></path></svg></span><span class=3D"sd-summary-text">Memory (RAM)</sp=
an><span class=3D"sd-summary-state-marker sd-summary-chevron-right"><svg ve=
rsion=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" height=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octic=
on-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M8.=
72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44 12 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.7=
51.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0=
 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></summary><div class=3D"sd-summary-content =
sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">There are two methods for specifying the amount o=
f memory/RAM:</p>
<ul class=3D"simple">
<li><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--mem</span></code> specifies how much memory <strong>p=
er node</strong></p></li>
<li><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--mem-per-cpu</span></code> specifies how much memory <=
strong>per core</strong>; use this option if specifying <code class=3D"docu=
tils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--ntasks</span></code></p></l=
i>
</ul>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">In both cases, specify memory with a number follo=
wed by <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">G</=
span></code> for gigabytes or <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">M</span></code> for megabytes.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Example:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell14" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --m=
em-per-cpu=3D3G</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell14">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">If your job submission script does not specify ho=
w much memory your job requires, then the default setting is 3110 MB of mem=
ory per core.  For a job specifying 10 cores and not specifying the memory =
requirements, Slurm will allocate 31100 MB (~30.3 GB)in total.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The memory that is allocated to a job via this se=
tting creates a <strong>hard upper limit</strong>; an application cannot ac=
cess memory beyond what Slurm reserves. Jobs that try to access more memory=
 than allocated will be terminated.  To determine the amount of memory need=
ed, <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwester=
n.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#ex=
ample-script">run a test job</a> with higher memory limits, and then set yo=
ur memory requirements to approximately 110% of the memory used by the test=
 job to account for variation across jobs.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">There is a special setting to request the entire =
memory of the computer.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell15" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --m=
em=3D0</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell15">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">How much memory this ends up being will depend on=
 what <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwest=
ern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#=
schedulable-resources">generation of compute node</a> the job is assigned t=
o.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">If a job requests more memory than is available o=
n any of the compute nodes available in that partition, then the job will b=
e rejected with the following message:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-default notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell16" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"n">srun</span=
><span class=3D"p">:</span> <span class=3D"n">error</span><span class=3D"p"=
>:</span> <span class=3D"n">Unable</span> <span class=3D"n">to</span> <span=
 class=3D"n">allocate</span> <span class=3D"n">resources</span><span class=
=3D"p">:</span> <span class=3D"n">Requested</span> <span class=3D"n">node</=
span> <span class=3D"n">configuration</span> <span class=3D"ow">is</span> <=
span class=3D"ow">not</span> <span class=3D"n">available</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell16">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Jobs requesting high amounts of memory may only b=
e able to run on more recent <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https:=
//rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?ut=
m_source=3Dchatgpt.com#schedulable-resources">generations of compute node</=
a>, which may mean it takes longer for the required resources for the job t=
o become available.</p>
</div>
</details><details class=3D"sd-sphinx-override sd-dropdown sd-card sd-mb-3"=
>
<summary class=3D"sd-summary-title sd-card-header">
<span class=3D"sd-summary-icon"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=
=3D"1.0em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octicon-note" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-=
hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 3.75C0 2.784.784 2 1.75 2h12.5c.966 0 1.75.78=
4 1.75 1.75v8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 14H1.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 12.25Zm1.75=
-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h12.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v=
-8.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25ZM3.5 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75h7a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1=
.5h-7a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75Zm.75 2.25h4a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-4a.75.75 0 0 1 0=
-1.5Z"></path></svg></span><span class=3D"sd-summary-text">Standard Output/=
Error</span><span class=3D"sd-summary-state-marker sd-summary-chevron-right=
"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" height=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon=
 sd-octicon-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path=
 d=3D"M8.72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44 12 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .01=
8-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.=
75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></summary><div class=3D"sd-summary=
-content sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">There are two output streams from a job: standard=
 output and standard error.  These output streams can be written to separat=
e files or the same file.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To send the output to separate files, use:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell17" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --o=
utput=3D&lt;name of file&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --error=3D&lt;name of file&gt;</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell17">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To send both the <em>standard output</em>  and <e=
m>standard error</em> to a single file, use only <code class=3D"docutils li=
teral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">-o</span></code>/<code class=3D"docu=
tils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--output</span></code> and om=
it <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--error=
</span></code>:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell18" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --o=
utput=3D&lt;name of file&gt;</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell18">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The files will be created in the directory from w=
hich you submit the job.  To direct the output to a different, already crea=
ted, directory, include the path as part of the filename.  A filename must =
be specified; a directory alone will not work.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">If you include neither <code class=3D"docutils li=
teral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--output</span></code> nor <code cla=
ss=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">-error</span></code=
>, Slurm will write both the standard output and standard error from your j=
ob in a file called</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-default notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell19" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"n">slurm</spa=
n><span class=3D"o">-&lt;</span><span class=3D"n">slurm</span> <span class=
=3D"n">jobid</span><span class=3D"o">&gt;.</span><span class=3D"n">out</spa=
n>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell19">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">where <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate=
"><span class=3D"pre">&lt;slurm</span> <span class=3D"pre">jobid&gt;</span>=
</code> is the ID given to your job by Slurm. You can replicate this defaul=
t naming scheme yourself by providing the following option:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell20" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --o=
utput=3Dslurm-%j.out</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell20">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">In addition to <code class=3D"docutils literal no=
translate"><span class=3D"pre">%j</span></code>, which will add the job id =
to the name of the output file, there is also <code class=3D"docutils liter=
al notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">%x</span></code> which will add the job=
 name to the name of the output file.</p>
</div>
</details><details class=3D"sd-sphinx-override sd-dropdown sd-card sd-mb-3"=
>
<summary class=3D"sd-summary-title sd-card-header">
<span class=3D"sd-summary-icon"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=
=3D"1.0em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octicon-note" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-=
hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 3.75C0 2.784.784 2 1.75 2h12.5c.966 0 1.75.78=
4 1.75 1.75v8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 14H1.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 12.25Zm1.75=
