ry-content sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To specify a specific generation of compute nodes=
 for your job, include a <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span=
 class=3D"pre">-C</span></code>/<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate=
"><span class=3D"pre">--constraint</span></code> option in the job submissi=
on script:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell23" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --c=
onstraint=3D&lt;name of compute node generation&gt;</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell23">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Compute node generations on Quest have names like=
 <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">quest14</=
span></code>; see <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.=
it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3D=
chatgpt.com#schedulable-resources">generations of compute nodes</a> for the=
 current options.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">If the job is requesting multiple nodes, and you =
would like all the compute nodes to be of the same generation and not a com=
bination of generations, then you can specify this with a command such as:<=
/p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell24" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --c=
onstraint=3D"[quest10|quest11|quest12|quest13|quest14]"</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell24">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">This would allow all of the nodes to be of any of=
 the four specified generations, but require all of them to be of the same =
generation.  This is recommended for jobs that are parallelized using MPI.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><spa=
n class=3D"pre">--constraint</span></code> is also used to specify specific=
 types of GPU cards. See the <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https:=
//rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/gpu/gpu.html#multi-=
gpu-jobs"><span class=3D"std std-ref">GPU page</span></a> for more informat=
ion.</p>
</div>
