<tbody>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Request GPUs</p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--gres=3Dname[[:type]:count]</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">The =E2=80=9Cname=E2=80=9D field will always =
be <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">gpu</sp=
an></code>. The =E2=80=9Ctype=E2=80=9D is an optional classification for th=
e resource (e.g. a100, h100, a30, l40s). Please note that when submitting t=
o <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">gengpu</=
span></code> if the exact GPU card is not important for your job, please om=
it this option as it will result in lower wait times when matching the job =
to a GPU resource. The =E2=80=9Ccount=E2=80=9D field is the number of GPU c=
ards with a default value of 1.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Job array</p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--array=3D&lt;array</span> <span class=3D"pre">indexes&=
gt;</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Submit a job array, a type of submission whic=
h will launch multiple jobs to be executed with identical parameters. The i=
ndexes specification identifies what array index values should be used. Mul=
tiple values may be specified using a comma separated list and/or a range o=
f values with a =E2=80=9C-=E2=80=9D separator. For example, <code class=3D"=
docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--array=3D0-15</span></co=
de> or <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--a=
rray=3D0,6,16-32</span></code>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Copy environment</p></=
td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--export=3DALL</span></code> (default) <br> <code class=
=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--export=3DNONE</span=
></code> ## to not export environment</p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Optional: Default is to export ALL environmen=
tal settings from the submission environment to the runtime environment.</p=
></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Copy environment variab=
le</p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--export=3D&lt;variable[=3Dvalue][,variable2=3Dvalue2[,=
=E2=80=A6]]&gt;</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Example: <code class=3D"docutils literal notr=
anslate"><span class=3D"pre">--export=3DEDITOR,ARG1=3Dtest</span></code> <b=
r> In this example, the propagated environment will only contain the variab=
le <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">EDITOR<=
/span></code> from the user=E2=80=99s environment, <code class=3D"docutils =
literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">SLURM_*</span></code> environment =
variables, and <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"=
pre">ARG1=3Dtest</span></code>.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Job dependency</p></td=
>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--dependency=3Dafter:jobID[:jobID=E2=80=A6]</span></cod=
e> <br> <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--=
dependency=3Dafterok:jobID[:jobID=E2=80=A6]</span></code> <br> <code class=
=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--dependency=3Daftern=
otok:jobID[:jobID=E2=80=A6]</span></code> <br> <code class=3D"docutils lite=
ral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--dependency=3Dafterany:jobID[:jobID=
=E2=80=A6]</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">After the specified jobs start or are cancell=
ed. <br> This job can begin execution after the specified jobs have success=
fully executed (ran to completion with an exit code of zero). <br> This job=
 can begin execution after the specified jobs have terminated in some faile=
d state (non-zero exit code, node failure, timed out, etc). <br> This job c=
an begin execution after the specified jobs have terminated. This is the de=
fault dependency type.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Defer job until the spe=
cified time</p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--begin=3D&lt;date/time&gt;</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Submit the batch script to the Slurm controll=
er immediately, like normal, but tell the controller to defer the schedulin=
g of the job until the specified time. <br> Time may be of the form HH:MM:S=
S to run a job at a specific time of day (seconds are optional).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Node exclusive job</p>=
</td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">--exclusive</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">The job is allocated all CPUs and GRES on all=
 requested nodes, but is only allocated as much memory as it requested. To =
request all the memory on the allocated nodes as well, use <code class=3D"d=
ocutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--mem=3D0</span></code>.</=
p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Instead of specifying h=
ow many nodes you want, you could request a specific set of compute nodes. =
This cannot be used in combination with the <code class=3D"docutils literal=
 notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--nodes</span></code> setting</p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">-w</span></code>,<code class=3D"docutils literal notran=
slate"><span class=3D"pre">--nodelist=3D&lt;node1[,node2[,...]]&gt;</span><=
/code> <br> <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre=
">-F</span></code>, <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span clas=
s=3D"pre">--nodefile=3D&lt;node</span> <span class=3D"pre">file&gt;</span><=
/code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Request a specific list of hosts. The job wil=
l contain all of these hosts and possibly additional hosts as needed to sat=
isfy resource requirements</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
