 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 =
6.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></summary><div class=3D"sd-s=
ummary-content sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Slurm implements a multi-factor priority scheme f=
or ordering the queue of jobs waiting to be run. The <code class=3D"docutil=
s literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sprio</span></code> command is u=
sed to see the contribution of different factors to a pending job=E2=80=99s=
 scheduling priority.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">sprio</span></code> command can be helpful to get an id=
ea of where your jobs might be in the overall queue of pending jobs. Howeve=
r, we caution against using it as a tool to estimate specific wait times. T=
he high-performance computing systems are complex and have many different c=
omponents that impact when jobs will run. This leads to variation in wait t=
ime. Similar to reservations at a restaurant, <code class=3D"docutils liter=
al notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sprio</span></code> can be helpful to t=
ell you that you=E2=80=99re 1 of the next 10 groups to get a table, but it =
doesn=E2=80=99t necessarily mean that you=E2=80=99ll be seated in the next =
5 minutes.</p>
<div class=3D"pst-scrollable-table-container" tabindex=3D"-1"><table class=
=3D"table">
<thead>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><th class=3D"head"><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Command<=
/p></th>
<th class=3D"head"><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Description</p></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class=3D"row-even"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutil=
s literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sprio</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Show scheduling priority for all pending jobs=
 for the user</p></td>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"row-odd"><td><p class=3D"sd-card-text"><code class=3D"docutils=
 literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sprio</span> <span class=3D"pre">=
-j</span> <span class=3D"pre">&lt;jobid&gt;</span></code></p></td>
<td><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Show scheduling priority of the defined job</=
p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">For running jobs, you can see the starting priori=
ty using <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">c=
heckjob</span> <span class=3D"pre">&lt;jobid&gt;</span></code> command.</p>
</div>
</details></section>
<section id=3D"special-types-of-job-submissions">
<h2>Special Types of Job Submissions<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"https:/=
/rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm=
_source=3Dchatgpt.com#special-types-of-job-submissions" title=3D"Link to th=
is heading">#</a></h2>
<p>In this section, we provide details and examples of how to use Slurm to =
run:</p>
<ul class=3D"simple">
<li><p>Interactive jobs where the user has access to the allocated compute =
resources to run commands interactively</p></li>
<li><p>Job arrays that submit multiple jobs using the same job submission s=
cript</p></li>
<li><p>Jobs that depend on other jobs completing first</p></li>
</ul>
<details class=3D"sd-sphinx-override sd-dropdown sd-card sd-mb-3" id=3D"slu=
rm-interactive-jobs">
<summary class=3D"sd-summary-title sd-card-header">
<span class=3D"sd-summary-icon"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=
=3D"1.0em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octicon-note" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-=
hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 3.75C0 2.784.784 2 1.75 2h12.5c.966 0 1.75.78=
4 1.75 1.75v8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 14H1.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 12.25Zm1.75=
-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h12.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v=
-8.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25ZM3.5 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75h7a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1=
.5h-7a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75Zm.75 2.25h4a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-4a.75.75 0 0 1 0=
-1.5Z"></path></svg></span><span class=3D"sd-summary-text">Interactive Jobs=
</span><span class=3D"sd-summary-state-marker sd-summary-chevron-right"><sv=
g version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" height=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-o=
cticon-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D=
"M8.72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44 12 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.0=
42.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.75.75=
 0 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></summary><div class=3D"sd-summary-cont=
ent sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">This section explains how to start interactive jo=
bs from the command line on the Quest login nodes.</p>
<div class=3D"admonition tip">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Tip</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://r=
cdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/ondemand/ondemand.html#quest-onde=
mand"><span class=3D"std std-ref">Quest OnDemand</span></a> provides a grea=
t alternative for launching interactive jobs through your web browser.</p>
</div>
<p class=3D"rubric" id=3D"jobs-without-guis">Jobs without GUIs</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To launch an interactive job in order to run
an application <em>without</em> a GUI, use either the
<a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/srun.html=
" target=3D"_blank"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span clas=
s=3D"pre">srun</span></code> <svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D=
"1.0em" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-hidden=3D"true" style=3D"display: inline=
-block; vertical-align: middle; fill: currentColor;"><path d=3D"M3.75 2h3.5=
a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-3.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h8.5a.2=
5.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v3.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 12.25 14h-8.=
5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 2 12.25v-8.5C2 2.784 2.784 2 3.75 2Zm6.854-1h4.146a.25.25=
 0 0 1 .25.25v4.146a.25.25 0 0 1-.427.177L13.03 4.03 9.28 7.78a.751.751 0 0=
 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042l3.75-3.75-1.543-1.543A.25.25 0 0 1 1=
0.604 1Z"></path></svg></a> or <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"http=
s://slurm.schedmd.com/salloc.html" target=3D"_blank"><code class=3D"docutil=
s literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">salloc</span></code> <svg versio=
n=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D"1.0em" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-hidde=
n=3D"true" style=3D"display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; fill: cu=
rrentColor;"><path d=3D"M3.75 2h3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-3.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.2=
5.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h8.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5=
 0v3.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 12.25 14h-8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 2 12.25v-8.5C2 2.784 2=
.784 2 3.75 2Zm6.854-1h4.146a.25.25 0 0 1 .25.25v4.146a.25.25 0 0 1-.427.17=
7L13.03 4.03 9.28 7.78a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042l3=
.75-3.75-1.543-1.543A.25.25 0 0 1 10.604 1Z"></path></svg></a>
command instead of <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=
=3D"pre">sbatch</span></code>.</p>
<p class=3D"rubric" id=3D"id3"><span id=3D"srun"></span>srun</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">If you use <code class=3D"docutils literal notran=
slate"><span class=3D"pre">srun</span></code> to run an interactive job, Sl=
urm will
automatically launch a terminal session on the compute node after it
schedules the job and the job starts.</p>
<div class=3D"admonition warning">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Warning</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">When using <a class=3D"reference external" href=
=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/srun.html" target=3D"_blank"><code class=3D"d=
ocutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">srun</span></code> <svg ve=
rsion=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D"1.0em" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" aria-h=
idden=3D"true" style=3D"display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; fill=
: currentColor;"><path d=3D"M3.75 2h3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-3.5a.25.25 0 0 =
0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h8.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-3.5a.75.75 0 0 1=
 1.5 0v3.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 12.25 14h-8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 2 12.25v-8.5C2 2.7=
84 2.784 2 3.75 2Zm6.854-1h4.146a.25.25 0 0 1 .25.25v4.146a.25.25 0 0 1-.42=
7.177L13.03 4.03 9.28 7.78a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.0=
42l3.75-3.75-1.543-1.543A.25.25 0 0 1 10.604 1Z"></path></svg></a>, if you =
lose your connection to Quest, the interactive job will terminate.</p>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Instead of writing a job submission script as you=
 would do for a batch job, for an interactive job, you can specify the key =
options as part of the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span c=
lass=3D"pre">srun</span></code> command directly.  The same <a class=3D"ref=
erence internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest=
/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#slurm-options">option=
s</a> for <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">=
sbatch</span></code> can be used with <code class=3D"docutils literal notra=
nslate"><span class=3D"pre">srun</span></code>.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Example:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell38" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">[quser41 =
~]$ </span>srun<span class=3D"w"> </span>--nodes<span class=3D"o">=3D</span=
><span class=3D"m">1</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>--ntasks<span class=3D=
"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">1</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>--account=
<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;account_id&gt;<span class=3D"w"> </span>--m=
em<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;memory&gt;<span class=3D"w"> </span><span=
 class=3D"se">\ </span><span class=3D"c1"># continue next line</span>
<span class=3D"go">&gt; --partition=3D&lt;partition&gt; --time=3D&lt;hh:mm:=
ss&gt; --pty bash -l</span>
<span class=3D"go">srun: job 3201233 queued and waiting for resources</span=
>
<span class=3D"go">srun: job 3201233 has been allocated resources</span>
<span class=3D"go">----------------------------------------</span>
<span class=3D"go">srun job start: Mon Mar 14 13:25:41 CDT 2022</span>
<span class=3D"go">Job ID: 3201233</span>
<span class=3D"go">Username: abc123</span>
<span class=3D"go">Queue: short</span>
<span class=3D"go">Account: pXXXXX</span>
<span class=3D"go">----------------------------------------</span>
<span class=3D"go">The following variables are not</span>
<span class=3D"go">guaranteed to be the same in</span>
<span class=3D"go">prologue and the job run script</span>
<span class=3D"go">----------------------------------------</span>
<span class=3D"go">PATH (in prologue) : /usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/=
sbin:/usr/sbin:/usr/lpp/mmfs/bin:/opt/ibutils/bin</span>
<span class=3D"go">WORKDIR is: /home/&lt;netid&gt;</span>
<span class=3D"go">----------------------------------------</span>
<span class=3D"gp">[qnode0114 ~]$</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell38">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">In the example above, the initial command has bee=
n split across two lines due to space constraints in the documentation.  Th=
e command can be run on a single line.  <code class=3D"docutils literal not=
ranslate"><span class=3D"pre">quser41</span></code> is a login node, while =
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">qnode0114<=
/span></code> is a compute node.  <code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">--pty</span> <span class=3D"pre">bash</span></code>=
 indicates to start a bash shell on the compute node. Adding the option <co=
de class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">-l</span></co=
de> to the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre"=
>bash</span></code> command will start a <em>login</em> bash shell on the c=
ompute node. This means that the environment for the bash shell will be the=
 same as the one you have on the login nodes.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">You can stop your interactive session by entering=
 the command <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pr=
e">exit</span></code>.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell39" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">[qnode011=
4 ~]$ </span><span class=3D"nb">exit</span>
<span class=3D"gp">[quser41 ~]$</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell39">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"rubric" id=3D"id4"><span id=3D"salloc"></span>salloc</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Unlike <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslat=
e"><span class=3D"pre">srun</span></code>, <a class=3D"reference external" =
href=3D"https://slurm.schedmd.com/salloc.html" target=3D"_blank"><code clas=
s=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">salloc</span></code>=
 <svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D"1.0em" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16=
" aria-hidden=3D"true" style=3D"display: inline-block; vertical-align: midd=
le; fill: currentColor;"><path d=3D"M3.75 2h3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-3.5a.25=
.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h8.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-3.5a.75.=
75 0 0 1 1.5 0v3.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 12.25 14h-8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 2 12.25v-8=
.5C2 2.784 2.784 2 3.75 2Zm6.854-1h4.146a.25.25 0 0 1 .25.25v4.146a.25.25 0=
 0 1-.427.177L13.03 4.03 9.28 7.78a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-=
.018-1.042l3.75-3.75-1.543-1.543A.25.25 0 0 1 10.604 1Z"></path></svg></a> =
does <em>not</em> automatically launch a
terminal session on the compute node. Instead, after it schedules your
job, it will tell you the name of the compute node the job has been schedul=
ed on. Then you can run <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span =
class=3D"pre">ssh</span> <span class=3D"pre">qnodeXXXX</span></code> to dir=
ectly connect to the compute
node. If you lose connection to your interactive session started with <code=
 class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">salloc</span></=
code>, the interactive job will <strong>not</strong> terminate.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Example:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell40" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">[quser41 =
~]$ </span>salloc<span class=3D"w"> </span>--nodes<span class=3D"o">=3D</sp=
an><span class=3D"m">1</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>--ntasks<span class=
=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">1</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>--acco=
unt<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;account_id&gt;<span class=3D"w"> </span>=
--mem<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;memory&gt;<span class=3D"w"> </span>--=
partition<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;partition&gt;<span class=3D"w"> </=
span>--time<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;hh:mm:ss&gt;
<span class=3D"go">salloc: Pending job allocation 276305</span>
<span class=3D"go">salloc: job 276305 queued and waiting for resources</spa=
n>
<span class=3D"go">salloc: job 276305 has been allocated resources</span>
<span class=3D"go">salloc: Granted job allocation 276305</span>
<span class=3D"go">salloc: Waiting for resource configuration</span>
<span class=3D"go">salloc: Nodes qnode0114 are ready for job</span>
<span class=3D"gp">[quser41 ~]$ </span>ssh<span class=3D"w"> </span>qnode01=
14
<span class=3D"go">Warning: Permanently added 'qnode0114,172.20.134.29' (EC=
DSA) to the list of known hosts.</span>
<span class=3D"gp">[qnode0114 ~]$</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell40">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">In the example above, <code class=3D"docutils lit=
eral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">quser41</span></code> is a login node=
, and <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">qnod=
e0114</span></code> is a compute node.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">You can stop your interactive session by entering=
 the command <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pr=
e">scancel</span> <span class=3D"pre">&lt;slurm-jobid&gt;</span></code>.</p=
>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell41" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">[qnode011=
4 ~]$ </span>scancel<span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"m">276305</spa=
n>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell41">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"rubric" id=3D"jobs-with-guis">Jobs with GUIs</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To launch an interactive job in order to run
an application <em>with</em> a GUI, first you need to connect to Quest usin=
g an
application with X11 forwarding support. We recommend using <a class=3D"ref=
erence internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest=
/user-guide/login/login-quest.html#connect-with-fastx-desktop-client"><span=
 class=3D"std std-ref">FastX</span></a>.
Once you have connected to Quest with X11 forwarding enabled, you can
then use either the
<a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.ed=
u/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#srun">=
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">srun</span=
></code></a> or <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it=
.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dch=
atgpt.com#salloc"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=
=3D"pre">salloc</span></code></a>
command with the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=
=3D"pre">--x11</span></code> option added.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Examples:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell42" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
srun<span class=3D"w"> </span>--x11<span class=3D"w"> </span>--nodes<span c=
lass=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">1</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>--=
ntasks<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">1</span><span class=3D"=
w"> </span>--account<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;account_id&gt;<span cla=
ss=3D"w"> </span>--mem<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;memory&gt;<span class=
=3D"w"> </span>--partition<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;partition&gt;<spa=
n class=3D"w"> </span>--time<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>&lt;hh:mm:ss&gt;<sp=
an class=3D"w"> </span>--pty<span class=3D"w"> </span>bash<span class=3D"w"=
> </span>-l
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell42">
