-8.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25ZM3.5 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 .75-.75h7a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1=
.5h-7a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75Zm.75 2.25h4a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-4a.75.75 0 0 1 0=
-1.5Z"></path></svg></span><span class=3D"sd-summary-text">Dependent Jobs</=
span><span class=3D"sd-summary-state-marker sd-summary-chevron-right"><svg =
version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" height=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-oct=
icon-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M=
8.72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44 12 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042=
.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.75.75 0=
 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></summary><div class=3D"sd-summary-conten=
t sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Dependent jobs are a series of jobs which run or =
wait to run conditional on the state of another job. For instance, you may =
submit two jobs and you want the first job to complete successfully before =
the second job runs.  This is helpful if one job needs to produce a data fi=
le or other output file that is an input to another job.  In order to submi=
t this type of workflow, you pass <code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">sbatch</span></code> the jobid of the job that need=
s to finish before this job starts via the command line argument:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-default notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell48" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"o">--</span><=
span class=3D"n">dependency</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=
=3D"n">afterok</span><span class=3D"p">:</span><span class=3D"o">&lt;</span=
><span class=3D"n">jobid</span><span class=3D"o">&gt;</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell48">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">You can manually submit a series of jobs, but it =
is helpful to write all of your <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate=
"><span class=3D"pre">sbatch</span></code> submission commands in a bash sc=
ript and pass the job IDs programmatically.  In order to be able to capture=
 and pass the job ID of one job to the next, save the output of a call to <=
code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sbatch</spa=
n></code> in a variable.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Here is an example submitting 3 jobs in sequence,=
 where each job depends on the previous job completing before it runs.  Thi=
s example uses the same job submission script, <code class=3D"docutils lite=
ral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">example_submit.sh</span></code> for ea=
ch job, but this is not required.  You can use different submission scripts=
 with different resource requests for each job.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Example: <code class=3D"docutils literal notransl=
ate"><span class=3D"pre">wrapper_script.sh</span></code></p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell49" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"ch">#!/bin/bash=
</span>
<span class=3D"c1"># submit the first job: no special options because it's =
the first job</span>
<span class=3D"nv">jid0</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"k"=
>$(</span>sbatch<span class=3D"w"> </span>--parsable<span class=3D"w"> </sp=
an>example_submit.sh<span class=3D"k">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># submit the second job: dependent on the first job with=
 ID stored in jid0</span>
<span class=3D"nv">jid1</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"k"=
>$(</span>sbatch<span class=3D"w"> </span>--parsable<span class=3D"w"> </sp=
an>--dependency<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>afterok:<span class=3D"si">${</s=
pan><span class=3D"nv">jid0</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D=
"w"> </span>--export<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"nv">DEPENDEN=
TJOB</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span cl=
ass=3D"nv">jid0</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>=
example_submit.sh<span class=3D"k">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># submit the third job: dependent on the second job with=
 ID stored in jid1</span>
<span class=3D"nv">jid2</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"k"=
>$(</span>sbatch<span class=3D"w"> </span>--parsable<span class=3D"w"> </sp=
an>--dependency<span class=3D"o">=3D</span>afterok:<span class=3D"si">${</s=
pan><span class=3D"nv">jid1</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D=
"w"> </span>--export<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"nv">DEPENDEN=
TJOB</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span cl=
ass=3D"nv">jid1</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"w"> </span>=
example_submit.sh<span class=3D"k">)</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell49">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The variables <code class=3D"docutils literal not=
ranslate"><span class=3D"pre">jid0</span></code>, <code class=3D"docutils l=
iteral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">jid1</span></code>, and <code class=
=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">jid2</span></code> wi=
ll contain the job ID that Slurm assigns each job.</p>
<div class=3D"admonition tip">
<p class=3D"admonition-title">Tip</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Anything you can tell Slurm via <code class=3D"do=
cutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span></code> in th=
e submission script itself you can also pass to <code class=3D"docutils lit=
eral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sbatch</span></code> via the command =
line.</p>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong><code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">example_submit.sh</span></code></strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell50" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"ch">#!/bin/bash=
</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --account=3D&lt;account_id&gt;  ## Required: you=
r Slurm account name, i.e. eXXXX, pXXXX or bXXXX</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --partition=3D&lt;partition&gt; ## Required: buy=
in, short, normal, long, gengpu, genhimem, etc.</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --time=3D&lt;HH:MM:SS&gt;       ## Required: How=
 long will the job need to run?  Limits vary by partition</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --nodes=3D&lt;#&gt;             ## How many comp=
uters/nodes do you need? Usually 1</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=3D&lt;#&gt;   ## How many CPUs=
 or processors do you need on per computer/node? (default value 1)</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --mem=3D&lt;#G&gt;              ## How much RAM =
do you need per computer/node? G =3D gigabytes</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --output=3Djob_%A.out     ## include the job ID =
in the output file name</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># very simple job to just print information to the outpu=
t file</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># print the date and time to the output file</span>
date

<span class=3D"c1"># print out the ID of the job this one was dependent on<=
/span>
<span class=3D"k">if</span><span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"o">[[</=
span><span class=3D"w"> </span>-z<span class=3D"w"> </span><span class=3D"s=
2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">DEPENDENTJOB</spa=
n><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"w"> =
</span><span class=3D"o">]]</span><span class=3D"p">;</span><span class=3D"=
w"> </span><span class=3D"k">then</span>
<span class=3D"w">    </span><span class=3D"nb">echo</span><span class=3D"w=
"> </span><span class=3D"s2">"First job in workflow"</span>
<span class=3D"k">else</span>
<span class=3D"w">    </span><span class=3D"nb">echo</span><span class=3D"w=
"> </span><span class=3D"s2">"Job started after "</span><span class=3D"w"> =
</span><span class=3D"nv">$DEPENDENTJOB</span>
<span class=3D"k">fi</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell50">
