content sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Location of error: <br>
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</s=
pan> <span class=3D"pre">--account=3D&lt;account_id&gt;</span></code> <br>
or <br>
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</s=
pan> <span class=3D"pre">-A</span> <span class=3D"pre">&lt;account&gt;</spa=
n></code></p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Example of correct syntax: <br>
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</s=
pan> <span class=3D"pre">--account=3Dp12345</span></code> <br>
or <br>
<code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</s=
pan> <span class=3D"pre">-A</span> <span class=3D"pre">p12345</span></code>=
</p>
<hr class=3D"docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Possible issue</strong>: The script doesn=
=E2=80=99t have an <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=
=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span></code> line specifying account</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Fix</strong>: Confirm that <code class=3D=
"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"pre">--account=3D&lt;account_id&gt;</span></code> is in the script</p=
>
<hr class=3D"docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Possible issue</strong>: A typo in the <c=
ode class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--account=3D=
</span></code> or <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=
=3D"pre">-A</span></code> part of this <code class=3D"docutils literal notr=
anslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span></code> line</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Fix</strong>: Examine this line closely t=
o make sure the syntax is correct</p>
<hr class=3D"docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Possible issue</strong>: You are not a me=
mber of the Slurm account specified in your job submission script</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Fix</strong>: Confirm you have access to =
the resource by typing <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span c=
lass=3D"pre">groups</span></code> at
the command line on Quest. If the account ID you have specified in your
job submission script is not listed, you do not have access to the compute =
resource with the specified account ID. Use an account ID for a resource th=
at you have access to in your job
submission script.</p>
<hr class=3D"docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Possible issue</strong>: The error is on =
a line earlier in your job submission script which causes Slurm to stop rea=
ding your script before it reaches the <code class=3D"docutils literal notr=
anslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span class=3D"pre">--account=
=3D&lt;account_id&gt;</span></code> line</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Fix</strong>: Move the <code class=3D"doc=
utils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span class=
=3D"pre">--account=3D&lt;account_id&gt;</span></code> line to be immediatel=
y
after the line <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"=
pre">#!/bin/bash</span></code> and submit your job again. If this
generates a new error referencing a different line of your script, the
account line is correct and the mistake is elsewhere in your submission
script. To resolve the new error, follow the debugging suggestions for
the new error message.</p>
