<section id=3D"debugging-a-job-accepted-by-the-scheduler">
<h3>Debugging a Job Accepted by the Scheduler<a class=3D"headerlink" href=
=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slu=
rm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#debugging-a-job-accepted-by-the-scheduler"=
 title=3D"Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
<p>Once your job has been accepted, the Slurm scheduler will return a job I=
D number. After waiting in the queue, your job will run. To see the status =
of your job, use the command <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https:=
//rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?ut=
m_source=3Dchatgpt.com#sacct"><code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate">=
<span class=3D"pre">sacct</span> <span class=3D"pre">-X</span></code></a>.<=
/p>
<p>Not all job submission errors generate error messages; if the output fro=
m your job is unexpected or incorrect, there may be an issue with the submi=
ssion script. If your script=E2=80=99s required elements (<a class=3D"refer=
ence internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/u=
ser-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#opt-account">account</a=
>, <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern=
.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#par=
titions">partition</a>, <a class=3D"reference internal" href=3D"https://rcd=
sdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_sou=
rce=3Dchatgpt.com#opt-nodes">nodes</a>, <a class=3D"reference internal" hre=
f=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest/user-guide/slurm/sl=
urm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#opt-cores">cores</a>, and <a class=3D"ref=
erence internal" href=3D"https://rcdsdocs.it.northwestern.edu/systems/quest=
/user-guide/slurm/slurm.html?utm_source=3Dchatgpt.com#opt-time">wall time</=
a>) have been read successfully before Slurm encounters the error, your job=
 will still be accepted by the scheduler and run, just not the way you expe=
ct it to. Scripts with issues that don=E2=80=99t generate errors still need=
 to be debugged since the scheduler has ignored or auto-populated some of y=
our <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATC=
H</span></code> lines.</p>
<p>For jobs with mistakes that do not give error messages, you will need to=
 investigate if you notice something is wrong with how the job runs.</p>
<p>Common problems include:</p>
