<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To see the name of your job, run <code class=3D"d=
ocutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sacct</span> <span class=
=3D"pre">-X</span></code>. If the JOB NAME listed in the output is the firs=
t eight characters of the name of your submission script, Slurm has not rea=
d the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBA=
TCH</span></code> line for job name.</p>
<hr class=3D"docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Possible issue</strong>: Job script omits=
 or misspecified the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span cla=
ss=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span class=3D"pre">--job-name=3D&lt;jobname&gt;<=
/span></code> directive.<br>
<strong>Possible issue</strong>: A typo in the <code class=3D"docutils lite=
ral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--job-name=3D</span></code> or <code c=
lass=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">-J</span></code> =
part of this <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pr=
e">#SBATCH</span></code> line</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Fix</strong>: Examine this line closely t=
o make sure the syntax is correct</p>
<hr class=3D"docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Possible issue</strong>: The error is on =
a line earlier in your job submission script which causes Slurm to stop rea=
ding your script before it reaches the <code class=3D"docutils literal notr=
anslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span class=3D"pre">--job-name=
=3D&lt;jobname&gt;</span></code> line</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Fix</strong>: Move the <code class=3D"doc=
utils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span class=
=3D"pre">--job-name=3D&lt;jobname&gt;</span></code> line to be immediately =
after the line <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"=
pre">#!/bin/bash</span></code> and submit your job again. If this generates=
 a new error referencing a different line of your script, the account line =
is correct and the mistake is elsewhere in your submission script. To resol=
ve the new error, follow the debugging suggestions for the new error messag=
e.</p>
