<p class=3D"sd-card-text">The =E2=80=9CState=E2=80=9D field is the status o=
f your job when it finished. Jobs with a =E2=80=9CCOMPLETED=E2=80=9D state =
have run without system errors. Jobs with an =E2=80=9COUT_OF_ME+=E2=80=9D s=
tate have run out of memory and failed. =E2=80=9COUT_OF_ME+=E2=80=9D jobs n=
eed to request more memory in their job submission scripts to complete succ=
essfully.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">If the job you=E2=80=99re investigating is not re=
cent enough to be listed by <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><s=
pan class=3D"pre">sacct</span> <span class=3D"pre">-X</span></code>, add da=
te fields to the command to see jobs between specific start and end dates. =
For example, to see all jobs between September 15, 2019 and September 16, 2=
019:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-console notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre =
id=3D"codecell71" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"gp">$ </span>=
sacct<span class=3D"w"> </span>-X<span class=3D"w"> </span>--starttime<span=
 class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">091519</span><span class=3D"w"> </=
span>--endtime<span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"m">091619</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
