t of memory and failed, now what?</span><span class=3D"sd-summary-state-mar=
ker sd-summary-chevron-right"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" height=
=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octicon-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 =
24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M8.72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44 1=
2 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a.7=
5.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></su=
mmary><div class=3D"sd-summary-content sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Often a challenge that researchers face is that t=
he amount of memory required to run an initial job may be unknown. Running =
out of memory will cause the job to fail with an out of memory (OOM) error.=
</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">A good strategy is to run a test job to determine=
 how much memory your job needs, and then request that amount of memory + 1=
0% when submitting your full job. In the example below, you=E2=80=99ll see =
that we start by requesting all of the memory for a node. This may be much =
more memory than we need, but it gives us a starting point to ensure that t=
he job completes. After the job completes, we=E2=80=99ll use specific appli=
cations to see how much memory was actually used by the job and adjust acco=
rdingly.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To do this:</p>
<ol class=3D"arabic simple">
<li><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Create a test job by editing your job=E2=80=
=99s submission script to reserve all of the memory of the node it runs on<=
/p></li>
<li><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Run your test job</p></li>
<li><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Confirm your test job has completed successfu=
lly</p></li>
<li><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Use <code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">jobstats</span></code> to see how much memory your =
job actually used</p></li>
<li><p class=3D"sd-card-text">Submit your full job with new memory limits</=
p></li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>1. Create a test job</strong></p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To profile your job=E2=80=99s memory usage, creat=
e a test job by modifying your job=E2=80=99s submission script to include t=
he lines:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell72" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --m=
em=3D0</span>
<span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --nodes=3D1</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell72">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Setting <code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">--mem=3D0</span></code> reserves all of the memory =
on the node for your job; if you already have a <code class=3D"docutils lit=
eral notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">--mem=3D</span></code> directive in y=
our job submission script, comment it out. Now your job will not run out of=
 memory unless your job needs more memory than is available on the node.</p=
>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Setting <code class=3D"docutils literal notransla=
te"><span class=3D"pre">--nodes=3D1</span></code> reserves a single node fo=
r your job. For jobs that run on multiple nodes such as MPI-based programs,=
 request the number of nodes that your job utilizes. Be sure to specify a v=
alue for <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#=
SBATCH</span> <span class=3D"pre">--nodes=3D</span></code> or the cores you=
r job submission script reserves could end up on as many nodes as cores req=
uested. Be aware that by setting <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslat=
e"><span class=3D"pre">--mem=3D0</span></code>, you will be reserving all t=
he memory on each of those nodes that your cores are reserved on.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Run your test job</strong></p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Submit your test job to the cluster with the <cod=
e class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sbatch</span><=
/code> command. For interactive jobs, use <code class=3D"docutils literal n=
otranslate"><span class=3D"pre">srun</span></code> or <code class=3D"docuti=
ls literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">salloc</span></code>.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>Did your test job complete successfully?<=
/strong></p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">When your job has stopped running, use the <code =
class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">sacct</span> <sp=
an class=3D"pre">-X</span></code> command to confirm your job finished with=
 state =E2=80=9CCOMPLETED=E2=80=9D. If your test job finishes with an =E2=
=80=9COUT_OF_ME+=E2=80=9D state, confirm that you are submitting the modifi=
ed job submission script that requests all of the memory on the node. If th=
e =E2=80=9COUT_OF_ME+=E2=80=9D errors persist, your job may require more me=
mory than is available on the compute node it ran on. In this case, please =
email <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"mailto:quest-help%40northwest=
ern.edu" target=3D"_blank">quest-help<span>@</span>northwestern<span>.</spa=
n>edu <svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.0em" height=3D"1.0em" viewBox=3D"0 0 =
16 16" aria-hidden=3D"true" style=3D"display: inline-block; vertical-align:=
 middle; fill: currentColor;"><path d=3D"M3.75 2h3.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-3.=
5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v8.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h8.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-3.5=
a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v3.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 12.25 14h-8.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 2 12.=
25v-8.5C2 2.784 2.784 2 3.75 2Zm6.854-1h4.146a.25.25 0 0 1 .25.25v4.146a.25=
.25 0 0 1-.427.177L13.03 4.03 9.28 7.78a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0=
 0 1-.018-1.042l3.75-3.75-1.543-1.543A.25.25 0 0 1 10.604 1Z"></path></svg>=
</a> for assistance.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text"><strong>How much memory did your job actually use=
?</strong></p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">To see how much memory your job used, run the com=
mand: <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">jobs=
tats</span> <span class=3D"pre">&lt;test_job_id_number&gt;</span></code>. T=
