0 1 2 0Z"></path></svg></span><span class=3D"sd-summary-text">How much memo=
ry should I reserve in my job script?</span><span class=3D"sd-summary-state=
-marker sd-summary-chevron-right"><svg version=3D"1.1" width=3D"1.5em" heig=
ht=3D"1.5em" class=3D"sd-octicon sd-octicon-chevron-right" viewBox=3D"0 0 2=
4 24" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M8.72 18.78a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06L14.44=
 12 8.72 6.28a.751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018l6.25 6.25a=
.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-6.25 6.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0Z"></path></svg></span></=
summary><div class=3D"sd-summary-content sd-card-body docutils">
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">This question builds off of the process that we o=
utlined in the <code class=3D"docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"=
pre">My</span> <span class=3D"pre">job</span> <span class=3D"pre">ran</span=
> <span class=3D"pre">out</span> <span class=3D"pre">of</span> <span class=
=3D"pre">memory</span> <span class=3D"pre">and</span> <span class=3D"pre">f=
ailed,</span> <span class=3D"pre">now</span> <span class=3D"pre">what</span=
></code> section above. Once you have an idea of how much memory your job n=
eeds to run successfully, you can adjust your memory requirements to find t=
he best balance between resource needs and wait time.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">It=E2=80=99s a good idea to reserve slightly more=
 memory than your job utilized since the same job may require slightly diff=
erent amounts of memory depending on variations in data it processes in eac=
h run of the job. To correctly reserve memory for this job, edit your test =
job submission script to modify the <code class=3D"docutils literal notrans=
late"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span class=3D"pre">--mem=3D</span=
></code> directive to reserve 10% more than 60Gb in the job submission scri=
pt:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell74" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --m=
em=3D66G</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell74">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">For jobs that use MPI, remove the <code class=3D"=
docutils literal notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span clas=
s=3D"pre">--mem=3D</span></code> directive from your job submission script.=
 Now specify the amount of memory you=E2=80=99d like to reserve per core in=
stead. For example, if your job uses 100Gb of memory total and runs on 10 c=
ores, reserve 10Gb plus a safety factor per cpu:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight-bash notranslate"><div class=3D"highlight"><pre id=
=3D"codecell75" tabindex=3D"-1"><span></span><span class=3D"c1">#SBATCH --m=
em-per-cpu=3D11G</span>
</pre><button class=3D"copybtn o-tooltip--left" data-tooltip=3D"Copy" data-=
clipboard-target=3D"#codecell75">
      <svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class=3D"icon icon-tabler i=
con-tabler-copy" width=3D"44" height=3D"44" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" stroke-wi=
dth=3D"1.5" stroke=3D"#000000" fill=3D"none" stroke-linecap=3D"round" strok=
e-linejoin=3D"round">
  <title>Copy to clipboard</title>
  <path stroke=3D"none" d=3D"M0 0h24v24H0z" fill=3D"none"></path>
  <rect x=3D"8" y=3D"8" width=3D"12" height=3D"12" rx=3D"2"></rect>
  <path d=3D"M16 8v-2a2 2 0 0 0 -2 -2h-8a2 2 0 0 0 -2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2">=
</path>
</svg>
    </button></div>
</div>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">If it doesn=E2=80=99t matter how many nodes your =
cores are distributed on, you may remove the <code class=3D"docutils litera=
l notranslate"><span class=3D"pre">#SBATCH</span> <span class=3D"pre">--nod=
es=3D</span></code> directive as well.</p>
<p class=3D"sd-card-text">Be careful not to reserve significant amounts of =
memory beyond what your job requires as your job=E2=80=99s wait time will i=
ncrease. Reserving excessive memory also wastes shared resources that could=
 be used by other researchers.</p>
</div>
